  The source file identifies its earlier origin as XephyLon/immaterial-impulse,
  v0.32.0, dots/.config/quickshell/imi/modules/common/functions/edit_mode.js,
  original author XephyLon. Its upstream attribution is preserved in the file.
  Ryoku's NOTICE describes Stage Editor as based on Edit Mode of ii-p3drovfx
  by P3DROVFX and contributors (https://github.com/P3DROVFX/ii-p3drovfx),
  itself built on ii-vynx by vaguesyntax (https://github.com/vaguesyntax/ii-vynx)
  and illogical-impulse by end-4 (https://github.com/end-4/dots-hyprland).
  Ryoku modified the editor to use its desktop services and appearance.
  Nayori imports this file unchanged and adapts its history API in
  surfaces/desktop/DesktopWidgets.qml. The viewport, card and drawer geometry
  from that module also drives Nayori's editor preview. The host adapts the
  bindings of Ryoku EditModeChromeSurface.qml to Nayori tokens and services.
  services/desktop/StageSession.qml is adapted from Ryoku at the same snapshot:
  ryoku/shell/quickshell/shell/modules/stage/Singletons/StageSession.qml.
  Nayori instantiates it instead of using a singleton and connects it to the
  existing settings controller and monitor list.

